{"schema_version": 1, "request_hash": "dfac44766b8058b2f65020fa7ecb6d4572a45c09614cf09128ec547c6e8954b1", "response": {"id": "msg_011ChMu46tVpuyZtrYt8BkCk", "container": null, "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I changed the regex in `injection_guard.py` so `looks_like_injection` now flags \"Ignore all previous instructions\" and variants with extra spaces. I did not run it against any example text.\n\nThe project has no tests, and I'm not allowed to add test files. `run_tests` collected nothing, so the only checks were reading the pattern and ruff, which passed after the edit.\n\nThe new pattern allows any number of modifier words between \"ignore\" and \"instructions\". Any run of whitespace, including tabs and newlines, can separate the words. By reading, \"Please follow the instructions in the manual\" is still not flagged, because \"ignore\" has to come first.\n\nI added \"prior\", \"above\", \"the\", \"any\" and \"my\" to the modifier list, which goes beyond the issue's wording. Only whitespace variation is handled. Other ways of disguising the phrase, such as punctuation between words or lookalike characters, are not caught.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 5109, "output_tokens": 294, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}}}
