{"schema_version": 1, "request_hash": "b8e852181cd798efed42e01093ce373d35f303a5d18583b28f2b1e9009bba2a9", "response": {"id": "msg_011ChMu6XJEeNtfG3enCXAYc", "container": null, "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed `classify_intent` in `intent_classifier.py`, but no test covers the change. The project has no tests (pytest collects none), and I'm not allowed to add test files. Ruff passes, and I did not run the new code on any sample replies.\n\n- **Code fences:** it now takes the contents of a markdown fence (three backticks, with or without `json`) before parsing. Fenced jailbreak replies are now caught. Plain JSON replies still parse as before.\n- **Unreadable replies:** these now return `Verdict(blocked=True, intent=\"unknown\")`, so the message is held back. That covers a reply that is not JSON, JSON that is not an object, an object with no `intent`, and an `intent` that is not text. A reply that is not a string at all is treated the same way.\n- **Fence position:** a fence is found anywhere in the reply, and the contents of the first fence are the part that gets parsed.\n- **Matching:** intent strings are still compared exactly, with no case normalization, as before.\n\nThe test command is `python -m pytest`.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 6712, "output_tokens": 341, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}}}
